		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Beach Buggy Blitz (Android &amp; iOS)]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=29368#p29368"><![CDATA[
Beach Buggy Blitz, the latest mobile game by Vector Unit, uses Bullet for collision detection and rigid body physics.<br><ul><li>Bullet Physics Library version 2.79</li><li>Custom car physics</li><li>Custom water physics</li><li>Fixed time-step at 60hz</li></ul>Using single-precision floating point for performance, the infinite driving mechanic is achieved by keeping the player 'near' the origin.  When the player reaches a certain distance threshold from the origin, the procedural track system steers the track creation back towards the origin.<br><br>Here are the links and some screenshots:<br><br><a href="http://www.youtube.com/watch?feature=player_embedded&amp;v=YqDczawTsYw" class="postlink">Trailer (YouTube)</a><br><a href="http://www.vectorunit.com/beach-buggy-blitz" class="postlink">Web Page</a><br><a href="http://market.android.com/details?id=com.vectorunit.yellow" class="postlink">Google Play</a><br><a href="http://itunes.apple.com/us/app/beach-buggy-blitz/id558204510" class="postlink">App Store</a><br><br><img src="https://lh4.ggpht.com/fdJGVvHeCWbDiJY5ThGmszqn3Ped5NjjhujLwcyZ-pKYID6G3ZXByb4OsEO1cfrh0t3N=w705" class="postimage" alt="Image"><br><br><img src="https://lh5.ggpht.com/ct_Y-lLzZB1EWH9txEtSbFbWhDi0JUYAISZY3B9QV2dYUNeli4sXEYVA4qda7b4tbQ" class="postimage" alt="Image"><br><br><img src="https://lh6.ggpht.com/eZjPbTmIWJUOp1X0nj-PrOElY0uvSXGzmyxBmKtgUfDBme4IJ2O3FIkFs6Bxv22Zubo" class="postimage" alt="Image"><br><br><img src="https://lh3.ggpht.com/c1GrHkNtO3LuC9UEJ6V8sBP_LAM30BW6ZA9B__Fztrt_tjGdbgIS_2zkbnVA54hpHTk" class="postimage" alt="Image"><br><br><img src="https://lh3.ggpht.com/BO9kEfT0cgPsQ-Q_uhC0iXxCtubkpZXf2AbYaJPeyzdPwzM_NEHBA1FkMVnRGhYVlQ" class="postimage" alt="Image"><br><br><img src="https://lh4.ggpht.com/lWJgvB0qk6LDERooiM6w5JzXwi3CGCCifiRLW9c-DkRV5y2J62yuk3cuWVA0uw05JQ" class="postimage" alt="Image"><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=3518">rknoesel</a> — Thu Nov 29, 20